1. DEFINITIONS
"Licensor" means the copyright holder(s) who authorize this License for their contributions to the Erudior Engine, as identified in applicable copyright notices.
"Engine" means the original Erudior application/lesson-engine software in this repository that the Licensor has the right to license under these terms, excluding Third-Party Materials and independently licensed content.
"Engine Modification" means a modification, adaptation, translation or derivative of Engine source code, including changes to its operation, course rendering, assessments, records, integration or user interface, but excluding independent course materials, datasets, documents or artwork that merely use the Engine's published interfaces.
"Covered Product" means an application, service, website or other distributed or publicly offered product incorporating or running the Engine or an Engine Modification.
"Main Engine Repository" means https://github.com/Aziliz/erudior or its officially announced successor.
"Third-Party Materials" means components, dependencies, media or other materials licensed by someone other than the Licensor under their own terms.

2. PERMISSION
Subject to compliance with this License, the Licensor grants a worldwide, nonexclusive, royalty-free, revocable-on-breach license to use, copy, modify and redistribute the Engine and make Covered Products, in source and binary form. This license grants no ownership of the Engine, no patent rights beyond any rights required by applicable law, and no rights in Third-Party Materials.

3. REQUIRED ERUDIOR SPLASH AND ATTRIBUTION
Every Covered Product with a graphical launch or entry experience must visibly display the official Erudior splash screen when the product starts, before presenting its main experience, with the Erudior name and a readable "Powered by Erudior" attribution. The splash may be adapted to screen size and accessibility requirements but must not be obscured, falsified, disabled by default or represented as the Covered Product developer's own branding.
Until the official graphic asset is supplied in the Main Engine Repository, an accessible text splash showing "Powered by Erudior" and a link to https://erudior.com satisfies this condition. Once the official asset is made available, new releases of Covered Products must include it in its unaltered branding form, except for resizing and accessible alternatives.
Products without a graphical launch (for example, command-line tools or headless services) must display equivalent attribution in their startup output when practical and in their readily accessible documentation or About information.
This requirement does not apply to mere independent course files, worksheets or other content that does not incorporate the Engine.

4. ENGINE MODIFICATIONS MUST BE RETURNED
If you distribute a Covered Product containing an Engine Modification, or make it available for interaction by users over a network, you must:
(a) make the complete corresponding source code of your Engine Modifications available under this License, including the changes and build instructions necessary to reproduce those modifications;
(b) submit those Engine Modifications to the Main Engine Repository through a pull request or, where pull requests are unavailable, through a publicly accessible source repository and a notice to the Maintainers describing the changes;
(c) make the submission no later than the first distribution or publicly accessible deployment and keep the corresponding source available while that modified version remains offered.
The Maintainers are not required to merge or accept a contribution. A good-faith, accessible submission satisfies the return requirement; private modifications that are never distributed or made accessible to third parties do not trigger this section.
Submissions must be original or properly licensed; you must not include secrets, personal information or third-party proprietary code. When an upstream change cannot legally be shared, you must obtain a separate license before distributing or offering that modified Engine version.

5. NOTICES AND SEPARATE WORKS
Keep this License and applicable copyright notices with copies or derivatives of the Engine, identify your modifications, and provide the corresponding source location in product documentation.
Independent courses, textbooks, exam questions, user data, student records, and assets authored through the Engine are not assigned to the Licensor and are not subject to the Engine Modification submission requirement merely because they use Erudior course formats.
Third-Party Materials remain governed by their original licenses. Nothing in this License overrides those licenses or grants rights the Licensor does not own.

6. TRADEMARKS
The Erudior name and official splash artwork may be used only to comply with the attribution obligation and to identify the Engine accurately. No broader trademark license, endorsement or sponsorship is granted. Do not imply that the Licensor has approved, accredited or certified your Covered Product.

